# Mumbai Traffic — weekday collection (Linux / hosted server).
#
# Install with:   crontab scripts/crontab.example
# Inspect with:   crontab -l
#
# IMPORTANT: cron uses the SERVER's timezone. Set the box to IST so the windows
# line up:   sudo timedatectl set-timezone Asia/Kolkata
#
# Fields: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week  command
# day-of-week 1-5 = Monday–Friday.
#
# Every reading writes to the SQLite store (data/processed/traffic.db) and the
# summary the dashboard serves. Pick ONE option below.

REPO=/opt/mumbai_traffic
PY=$REPO/.venv/bin/python

# ============================================================================
# OPTION A — three fixed segment readings per weekday (lightest on the API).
# ============================================================================
# Morning office peak (09:00), evening office peak (18:45), inter-peak avg (14:00).
0 9  * * 1-5  cd $REPO && $PY -m src.data.collect_flow --n 50 --segment peak && $PY -m src.data.segment_summary >> $REPO/data/collect.log 2>&1
45 18 * * 1-5 cd $REPO && $PY -m src.data.collect_flow --n 50 --segment peak && $PY -m src.data.segment_summary >> $REPO/data/collect.log 2>&1
0 14 * * 1-5  cd $REPO && $PY -m src.data.collect_flow --n 50 --segment avg  && $PY -m src.data.segment_summary >> $REPO/data/collect.log 2>&1

# ============================================================================
# OPTION B — full-day adaptive loop: one launch at 06:00, then the process
# self-schedules readings every 10 min in peak windows / 15 min otherwise,
# until 23:00. (Comment out Option A above if you use this.)
# Preview the daily API-call estimate first:  $PY -m src.data.collect_day --dry-run
# ============================================================================
# 0 6 * * 1-5  cd $REPO && $PY -m src.data.collect_day --n 25 --until 23:00 >> $REPO/data/collect.log 2>&1

# ============================================================================
# OPTION C — pure-cron interval sampling (no long-running process). Every 10 min
# during peak hours, every 15 min otherwise; the collector auto-tags the segment.
# Keep the hour sets DISJOINT so a reading is not taken twice.
# ============================================================================
# */10 8-10,18-20   * * 1-5 cd $REPO && $PY -m src.data.collect_flow --n 25 && $PY -m src.data.segment_summary >> $REPO/data/collect.log 2>&1
# */15 6-7,11-17,21-22 * * 1-5 cd $REPO && $PY -m src.data.collect_flow --n 25 && $PY -m src.data.segment_summary >> $REPO/data/collect.log 2>&1
